Just a little advice out there for those who want to get a lot of experience for
only a small amount of work....if you try the pudding trick from sinks, be sure
the room is closed off and kick the damn thing to death.  

An Example (I'm still clearing puddings from this level):

An Elf, armed with a wand of fire and a blessed +0 Mjollnir decides to get to, 
oh, about level 12 or so in a hurry.  He inscribes Elbereth in all exits and in
one spot next to the sink with his wand of fire.  Then he kicks the sink.  
Pudding!  Unfortunately, Mjollnir is not rustproof and to my dismay it is now a
blessed -6 Mjollnir, and I now have about 20+ black puddings to clear away.
The only good news is that I reached level 11 and have gained quite a few
intrinsics.....:)

